(window.STEP_BOOK = window.STEP_BOOK || {})["R1"] = {"n":1,"level":"A1","t":"Reading Short Everyday Texts","lessons":[{"id":"1.1","t":"Main Idea of Short Texts","html":"<p><strong>Unit 1 · Lesson 1.1 · CEFR A1 · STEP link: Reading Comprehension (40%)</strong></p>\n<h3>Objectives</h3>\n<p>1. Identify what a short text is mostly about.</p>\n<p>2. Separate the main idea from a single detail.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الأهداف</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">١. أن يحدد الطالب الفكرة التي يدور حولها النص القصير في معظمه.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٢. أن يميّز بين الفكرة الرئيسة وتفصيلة واحدة من النص.</span></p>\n<h3>The Skill</h3>\n<p>The main idea is the most important point of a text — what the whole text is about. A detail is one small piece of information that supports the main idea.</p>\n<p>In short texts, the main idea is often in the first or the last sentence. The other sentences give examples, reasons or descriptions.</p>\n<p><strong>Typical STEP question stems:</strong></p>\n<p>▸ What is the text mainly about?</p>\n<p>▸ What is the main idea of the text?</p>\n<p>▸ Which sentence best describes the whole text?</p>\n<p>▸ The text is mostly about …</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">المهارة</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الفكرة الرئيسة هي أهم ما يريد النص قوله، أي الموضوع الذي يدور حوله النص كله، أما التفصيلة فهي معلومة صغيرة تدعم الفكرة الرئيسة. وفي النصوص القصيرة تأتي الفكرة الرئيسة غالبًا في الجملة الأولى أو الأخيرة.</span></p>\n<h3>Strategy</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>1. Read the title and the first sentence carefully.</p>\n<p>2. Ask: Who or what is the text about?</p>\n<p>3. Ask: What does the writer say about it again and again?</p>\n<p>4. Check the last sentence — it often repeats the main idea.</p>\n<p>5. Choose the option that covers the WHOLE text, not one sentence.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">اقرأ العنوان والجملة الأولى، واسأل: عمّ يتحدث النص؟ وما الفكرة التي تتكرر؟ ثم راجع الجملة الأخيرة، واختر الإجابة التي تشمل النص كله لا جملة واحدة منه.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Traps and Distractor Types</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>✗ Too narrow: the option is true but talks about only one detail.</p>\n<p>✗ Too broad: the option is about a much bigger topic than the text.</p>\n<p>✗ Not in the text: the option uses a word from the text but says something the text does not say.</p>\n<p>✗ Opposite: the option says the reverse of the text.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Worked Example (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>Example text: Our New Neighbour</strong></p>\n<p><em>(66 words)</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A new family moved into the house next to ours last week. The father is a doctor, and the mother teaches maths. They have two sons, Saud and Ziyad. Saud is nine, and Ziyad is six. On Friday, my mother made a cake for them. They were very happy. Now Ziyad and my little brother play together every afternoon. We like our new neighbours very much.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Example 1. What is the text mainly about?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. a new family next door B. a doctor's job</p>\n<p>C. a cake recipe D. a maths teacher</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The text talks about the family in every sentence.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> B, C and D are only small details.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The answer is A.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Example 2. Which is the best title for the text?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. Making a Cake B. Our Friendly New Neighbours</p>\n<p>C. Playing in the Afternoon D. Two Brothers at School</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The first and last sentences are about the new neighbours.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Option B covers the whole text.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The answer is B.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الجملتان الأولى والأخيرة تتحدثان عن الجيران الجدد، لذلك فهي الفكرة الرئيسة، والباقي تفاصيل.</span></p>","wu":"Worked example: Example 1 A · Example 2 B","quiz":[{"l":["Read each text and answer the questions. Choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","اقرأ كل نص ثم أجب عن الأسئلة التي تليه، واختر الإجابة الصحيحة من بين البدائل الأربعة.","Text 1 (Questions 1–5): A boy's morning routine before school","(68 words)","Faisal wakes up at six o'clock every morning. First, he washes his face and brushes his teeth. Then he puts on his school uniform. His mother makes eggs and bread for breakfast, and Faisal drinks a glass of milk. At half past six, he checks his school bag. At seven o'clock, the school bus comes, and Faisal says goodbye to his family. He is never late for school."],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"What is the text mainly about?","o":["Faisal's school bus driver","Faisal's favourite breakfast","Faisal's school uniform","Faisal's morning before school"],"k":3,"e":"[main idea] Every sentence tells what Faisal does in the morning before school.","h":"كل الجمل تصف صباح فيصل قبل المدرسة."},{"n":2,"s":"Which is the best title?","o":["Getting Ready for School","A Glass of Milk","A Late Student","My Mother's Kitchen"],"k":0,"e":"[best title] The text describes all the steps Faisal takes to get ready.","h":"العنوان يجب أن يشمل النص كله."},{"n":3,"s":"What time does Faisal wake up?","o":["at half past six","at seven o'clock","at six o'clock","at half past seven"],"k":2,"e":"[detail] The first sentence says he wakes up at six o'clock.","h":"الجملة الأولى تذكر الساعة السادسة."},{"n":4,"s":"What does Faisal do at half past six?","o":["He eats breakfast.","He checks his school bag.","He gets on the bus.","He brushes his teeth."],"k":1,"e":"[detail] The text says: At half past six, he checks his school bag.","h":"ابحث عن half past six."},{"n":5,"s":"Which sentence is the most important idea of the text?","o":["Faisal has the same routine every morning before school.","Faisal drinks a glass of milk.","The bus comes at seven.","Faisal's mother makes eggs."],"k":0,"e":"[main idea] The other options are small details; the main idea is his morning routine.","h":"الفكرة الرئيسة هي روتين فيصل الصباحي."}]},{"l":["Text 2 (Questions 6–10): A family picnic in a Riyadh park","(77 words)","Last Friday, my family had a picnic in Salam Park in Riyadh. We arrived at four o'clock in the afternoon. My father put a big carpet under a tree, and my mother opened the food boxes. We ate chicken, rice and fruit. After lunch, my brothers played football, and my sister and I fed the ducks near the lake. In the evening, the weather was cool and nice. It was a happy day for all of us."],"q":[{"n":6,"s":"What is the text mostly about?","o":["the ducks in Salam Park","a family's day out in a park","how to play football","the weather in Riyadh"],"k":1,"e":"[main idea] The whole text is about the family picnic.","h":"النص كله عن نزهة العائلة."},{"n":7,"s":"Which is the best title?","o":["A Happy Picnic in the Park","Feeding the Ducks","Chicken and Rice","A Big Carpet"],"k":0,"e":"[best title] Only this title covers all the activities of the day.","h":"العنوان الشامل للنص."},{"n":8,"s":"Where did the family sit?","o":["on a carpet under a tree","near the football field","in the car","inside a restaurant"],"k":0,"e":"[detail] My father put a big carpet under a tree.","h":"الأب وضع سجادة تحت شجرة."},{"n":9,"s":"What did the writer and her sister do after lunch?","o":["They played football.","They opened the food boxes.","They went home.","They fed the ducks."],"k":3,"e":"[detail] My sister and I fed the ducks near the lake.","h":"أطعمتا البط."},{"n":10,"s":"How did the family feel about the day?","o":["They were bored.","They were tired and angry.","They enjoyed it.","They wanted to leave early."],"k":2,"e":"[main idea] The last sentence says it was a happy day for all of them.","h":"الجملة الأخيرة: كان يومًا سعيدًا."}]},{"l":["Text 3 (Questions 11–15): A baby goat on a small farm","(72 words)","My uncle has a small farm near Qassim. Last week, a baby goat was born there. It is white with a black spot on its head. Its legs are long and thin, and it jumps everywhere. The baby goat drinks milk from its mother five times a day. My cousins call it Snowy. When we visited the farm, Snowy came to us and played with us. Everyone loves the new baby goat."],"q":[{"n":11,"s":"What is the text mainly about?","o":["a new baby goat on a farm","my uncle's job","how to drink milk","a trip to Qassim"],"k":0,"e":"[main idea] Most sentences describe the baby goat.","h":"معظم الجمل تصف الماعز الصغير."},{"n":12,"s":"What colour is the baby goat?","o":["black with a white spot","brown","white with a black spot","all white"],"k":2,"e":"[detail] It is white with a black spot on its head.","h":"أبيض وفيه بقعة سوداء."},{"n":13,"s":"How often does the goat drink milk?","o":["once a day","five times a day","twice a day","every hour"],"k":1,"e":"[detail] It drinks milk five times a day.","h":"خمس مرات يوميًا."},{"n":14,"s":"Which is the best title?","o":["My Uncle's House","Snowy, the New Baby Goat","Animals in Qassim","Long Legs"],"k":1,"e":"[best title] The text is about Snowy, the baby goat.","h":"العنوان عن الماعز سنوي."},{"n":15,"s":"Which sentence gives the main idea of the last part of the text?","o":["Everyone loves the new baby goat.","It is white with a black spot.","Its legs are long and thin.","My uncle has a small farm."],"k":0,"e":"[main idea] The last sentence sums up the feelings of the family.","h":"الجملة الأخيرة تلخص المشاعر."}]},{"l":["Text 4 (Questions 16–20): The new school cafeteria","(68 words)","Our school has a new cafeteria this year. It is big and bright, with fifty tables and blue chairs. The food is healthy. There are sandwiches, salads, fresh fruit and juice. There are no fizzy drinks or crisps. The cafeteria opens at nine o'clock, and the prices are low. A sandwich costs only five riyals. All the students like the new cafeteria, and the teachers eat there too."],"q":[{"n":16,"s":"What is the text mainly about?","o":["healthy salads","the teachers' lunch","the school's new cafeteria","low prices in shops"],"k":2,"e":"[main idea] The whole text describes the new cafeteria.","h":"النص كله يصف المقصف الجديد."},{"n":17,"s":"How many tables are there?","o":["fifteen","five","fifty","nine"],"k":2,"e":"[detail] It has fifty tables.","h":"خمسون طاولة."},{"n":18,"s":"Which food is NOT in the cafeteria?","o":["salads","fresh fruit","sandwiches","crisps"],"k":3,"e":"[NOT / EXCEPT] There are no fizzy drinks or crisps.","h":"لا توجد رقائق البطاطس."},{"n":19,"s":"How much is a sandwich?","o":["five riyals","nine riyals","fifteen riyals","fifty riyals"],"k":0,"e":"[detail] A sandwich costs only five riyals.","h":"خمسة ريالات."},{"n":20,"s":"Which is the best title?","o":["Blue Chairs","Teachers at Lunch","No Fizzy Drinks","A Healthy New Place to Eat"],"k":3,"e":"[best title] The title should cover the new, healthy cafeteria.","h":"عنوان شامل."}]},{"l":["Text 5 (Questions 21–25): Grandmother's herb garden","(71 words)","My grandmother has a small herb garden behind her house in Taif. She grows mint, basil and parsley. Every morning, she waters the plants with a green can. She does not use chemicals, so the herbs are clean and fresh. When we visit her, she puts fresh mint in our tea. Sometimes she gives us bags of herbs to take home. My grandmother says her garden makes her happy and healthy."],"q":[{"n":21,"s":"What is the text mostly about?","o":["making mint tea","Grandmother's herb garden","the city of Taif","a green watering can"],"k":1,"e":"[main idea] The text describes the garden and how Grandmother uses it.","h":"النص عن حديقة الجدة."},{"n":22,"s":"Where is the garden?","o":["behind her house","in front of the house","next to a school","on the roof"],"k":0,"e":"[detail] behind her house in Taif.","h":"خلف بيتها."},{"n":23,"s":"Why are the herbs clean?","o":["She washes them every day.","She buys them from a shop.","She does not use chemicals.","It rains a lot in Taif."],"k":2,"e":"[cause–effect] She does not use chemicals, so the herbs are clean.","h":"لا تستخدم مواد كيميائية."},{"n":24,"s":"What does Grandmother put in their tea?","o":["basil","fresh mint","parsley","sugar"],"k":1,"e":"[detail] she puts fresh mint in our tea.","h":"النعناع الطازج."},{"n":25,"s":"What is the main idea of the last sentence?","o":["Grandmother is very old.","Herbs are expensive.","Grandmother does not like visitors.","The garden is good for Grandmother."],"k":3,"e":"[main idea] She says her garden makes her happy and healthy.","h":"الحديقة مفيدة للجدة."}]},{"l":["Text 6 (Questions 26–30): A cat that sleeps all day","(69 words)","We have a big orange cat called Tiger. Tiger sleeps almost all day. In the morning, he sleeps on the sofa. At noon, he sleeps in a box near the window. In the afternoon, he sleeps on my bed. He only wakes up to eat his food and drink some water. At night, Tiger is suddenly very active. He runs around the house and plays with his toy mouse!"],"q":[{"n":26,"s":"What is the text mainly about?","o":["a toy mouse","a cat that sleeps a lot","an orange sofa","a box near the window"],"k":1,"e":"[main idea] Most sentences tell where and when Tiger sleeps.","h":"معظم الجمل عن نوم القط."},{"n":27,"s":"Which is the best title?","o":["My Bedroom","A Toy Mouse","Food and Water","Tiger, the Sleepy Cat"],"k":3,"e":"[best title] This title covers the main idea.","h":"عنوان شامل."},{"n":28,"s":"Where does Tiger sleep at noon?","o":["on the sofa","on my bed","in a box near the window","in the kitchen"],"k":2,"e":"[detail] At noon, he sleeps in a box near the window.","h":"عند الظهر في صندوق."},{"n":29,"s":"When is Tiger very active?","o":["in the morning","at noon","in the afternoon","at night"],"k":3,"e":"[detail] At night, Tiger is suddenly very active.","h":"في الليل."},{"n":30,"s":"Which sentence is a detail, NOT the main idea?","o":["Tiger sleeps almost all day.","The text is about Tiger's sleeping habits.","He plays with his toy mouse.","Tiger is a sleepy cat."],"k":2,"e":"[main idea] Playing with a toy mouse is one small detail.","h":"اللعب بالفأرة تفصيلة صغيرة."}]}],"n":30},{"id":"1.2","t":"Scanning for Names, Numbers, Times and Places","html":"<p><strong>Unit 1 · Lesson 1.2 · CEFR A1 · STEP link: Reading Comprehension (40%)</strong></p>\n<h3>Objectives</h3>\n<p>1. Scan short texts for names, numbers, times and places.</p>\n<p>2. Answer detail questions quickly without reading every word.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الأهداف</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">١. أن يمسح الطالب النص بسرعة بحثًا عن الأسماء والأرقام والأوقات والأماكن.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٢. أن يجيب عن أسئلة التفاصيل بسرعة دون قراءة كل كلمة.</span></p>\n<h3>The Skill</h3>\n<p>Scanning means moving your eyes quickly over a text to find one piece of information, such as a time, a price or a name. You do not read every word.</p>\n<p>Timetables, invitations, notices and screens are perfect for scanning because the information is organized in lines.</p>\n<p><strong>Typical STEP question stems:</strong></p>\n<p>▸ What time does … start?</p>\n<p>▸ Where is …?</p>\n<p>▸ How much does … cost?</p>\n<p>▸ Who …?</p>\n<p>▸ On which day …?</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">المهارة</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">المسح السريع يعني تحريك العين بسرعة على النص للعثور على معلومة واحدة مثل وقت أو سعر أو اسم دون قراءة كل كلمة، وهو مناسب للجداول والدعوات والإعلانات.</span></p>\n<h3>Strategy</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>1. Read the question first and underline the key word (time, name, place, number).</p>\n<p>2. Decide what the answer looks like: a number? a name with a capital letter? a time?</p>\n<p>3. Move your eyes quickly down the text to find that kind of word.</p>\n<p>4. Read the sentence or line around it carefully.</p>\n<p>5. Check that the answer matches the question exactly (day, time, a.m. / p.m.).</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">اقرأ السؤال أولًا وحدّد الكلمة المفتاحية، وتوقّع شكل الإجابة (رقم أو اسم أو وقت)، ثم حرّك عينيك بسرعة للعثور عليها، واقرأ السطر المحيط بها بعناية.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Traps and Distractor Types</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>✗ A similar number in the wrong line (e.g., 7:30 for another bus).</p>\n<p>✗ The right time but the wrong day.</p>\n<p>✗ A name that appears in the text but answers a different question.</p>\n<p>✗ Mixing up a.m. and p.m.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Worked Example (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>Example text: Notice: Swimming Lessons</strong></p>\n<p><em>(34 words)</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Swimming Lessons for Children (ages 7–12)</p>\n<p>Days: Sunday and Wednesday</p>\n<p>Time: 4:00 p.m. – 5:00 p.m.</p>\n<p>Place: City Sports Centre, Pool 2</p>\n<p>Price: 150 riyals a month</p>\n<p>Teacher: Coach Majed</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Example 1. Where are the lessons?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. in Pool 1 B. in Pool 2 C. at school D. at the beach</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The key word is Where → look for a place.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Place: City Sports Centre, Pool 2.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The answer is B.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Example 2. How much are the lessons?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. 12 riyals B. 50 riyals</p>\n<p>C. 150 riyals a month D. 150 riyals a week</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Look for a price.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Price: 150 riyals a month — check a month, not a week.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The answer is C.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">ابحث عن نوع المعلومة المطلوبة: مكان أو سعر، ثم تحقق من التفاصيل الصغيرة مثل a month وa week.</span></p>","wu":"Worked example: Example 1 B · Example 2 C","quiz":[{"l":["Read each text and answer the questions. Choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","اقرأ كل نص ثم أجب عن الأسئلة التي تليه، واختر الإجابة الصحيحة من بين البدائل الأربعة.","Text 1 (Questions 1–5): A Sunday school timetable","(63 words)","Sunday Timetable — Class 3B","7:15 – 8:00 Arabic (Mr. Khalid, Room 12)","8:00 – 8:45 English (Mr. Waleed, Room 14)","8:45 – 9:30 Maths (Mr. Sami, Room 12)","9:30 – 9:50 Break","9:50 – 10:35 Science (Mr. Fahad, Lab 2)","10:35 – 11:20 Art (Mr. Nasser, Art Room)","11:20 – 12:00 P.E. (Coach Omar, Gym)"],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"What time does English start?","o":["7:15","8:45","8:00","9:50"],"k":2,"e":"[detail] 8:00 – 8:45 English.","h":"ابحث عن English."},{"n":2,"s":"Who teaches Science?","o":["Mr. Sami","Mr. Khalid","Coach Omar","Mr. Fahad"],"k":3,"e":"[detail] Science (Mr. Fahad, Lab 2).","h":"ابحث عن Science."},{"n":3,"s":"Where is the Maths lesson?","o":["Room 14","Lab 2","Room 12","the Gym"],"k":2,"e":"[detail] Maths (Mr. Sami, Room 12).","h":"ابحث عن Maths."},{"n":4,"s":"How long is the break?","o":["forty-five minutes","ten minutes","twenty minutes","one hour"],"k":2,"e":"[detail] 9:30 – 9:50 is twenty minutes.","h":"من 9:30 إلى 9:50."},{"n":5,"s":"Which lesson is the last one of the day?","o":["Art","Science","Arabic","P.E."],"k":3,"e":"[detail] 11:20 – 12:00 P.E. is the last line.","h":"آخر سطر."}]},{"l":["Text 2 (Questions 6–10): A bus timetable from Jeddah to Makkah","(80 words)","SAPTCO Bus Timetable: Jeddah → Makkah","Bus 1 leaves 6:00 a.m. arrives 7:15 a.m. Price: 25 riyals","Bus 2 leaves 9:30 a.m. arrives 10:45 a.m. Price: 25 riyals","Bus 3 leaves 1:00 p.m. arrives 2:15 p.m. Price: 25 riyals","Bus 4 leaves 6:00 p.m. arrives 7:30 p.m. Price: 30 riyals","All buses leave from the Central Bus Station, Gate 4.","Children under 6 travel free."],"q":[{"n":6,"s":"When does Bus 2 leave?","o":["6:00 a.m.","9:30 a.m.","10:45 a.m.","1:00 p.m."],"k":1,"e":"[detail] Bus 2 leaves 9:30 a.m.","h":"سطر Bus 2."},{"n":7,"s":"How much is a ticket on Bus 4?","o":["30 riyals","25 riyals","6 riyals","4 riyals"],"k":0,"e":"[detail] Bus 4 … Price: 30 riyals.","h":"سطر Bus 4."},{"n":8,"s":"Which bus arrives at 2:15 p.m.?","o":["Bus 1","Bus 2","Bus 3","Bus 4"],"k":2,"e":"[detail] Bus 3 arrives 2:15 p.m.","h":"ابحث عن 2:15."},{"n":9,"s":"Where do the buses leave from?","o":["Gate 4 of the Central Bus Station","Gate 6 in Makkah","the airport","Bus Station 2"],"k":0,"e":"[detail] All buses leave from the Central Bus Station, Gate 4.","h":"مكان الانطلاق."},{"n":10,"s":"This timetable mainly tells passengers …","o":["how to drive to Makkah","when the buses leave and arrive","where to buy food","why the buses are late"],"k":1,"e":"[main idea] Every line gives leaving and arriving times.","h":"الجدول يبيّن مواعيد الانطلاق والوصول."}]},{"l":["Text 3 (Questions 11–15): A birthday party invitation card","(68 words)","You are invited!","Come to Reem's 10th birthday party.","Day: Thursday, 14 March","Time: 5:00 p.m. to 8:00 p.m.","Place: Reem's house, 22 Al-Nahda Street, Dammam","There will be games, a magic show and a big chocolate cake.","Please wear comfortable clothes because we will play outside in the garden.","Please tell Reem's mother, Mrs. Huda, if you can come. Phone: 055 123 4567"],"q":[{"n":11,"s":"Whose party is it?","o":["Reem's","Huda's","Nahda's","Dammam's"],"k":0,"e":"[detail] Reem's 10th birthday party.","h":"حفلة ريم."},{"n":12,"s":"How old will Reem be?","o":["fourteen","five","eight","ten"],"k":3,"e":"[detail] Reem's 10th birthday.","h":"العاشرة."},{"n":13,"s":"What time does the party finish?","o":["5:00 p.m.","8:00 p.m.","10:00 p.m.","7:00 p.m."],"k":1,"e":"[detail] 5:00 p.m. to 8:00 p.m.","h":"وقت الانتهاء."},{"n":14,"s":"What is the house number?","o":["14","10","55","22"],"k":3,"e":"[detail] 22 Al-Nahda Street.","h":"رقم المنزل 22."},{"n":15,"s":"Who should guests tell if they can come?","o":["Reem's teacher","Reem's mother","the magician","Reem's father"],"k":1,"e":"[detail] Please tell Reem's mother, Mrs. Huda.","h":"والدة ريم."}]},{"l":["Text 4 (Questions 16–20): A sports club's opening hours","(72 words)","Al-Nakheel Sports Club — Opening Hours","Saturday to Wednesday: 6:00 a.m. – 11:00 p.m.","Thursday: 6:00 a.m. – midnight","Friday: 2:00 p.m. – 11:00 p.m.","Swimming pool: closed every Monday for cleaning.","Football field: book at reception (100 riyals an hour).","Children's swimming lessons: Saturday and Tuesday, 4:00 p.m. – 5:00 p.m.","New members: get your free first week! Call 920 001 234."],"q":[{"n":16,"s":"What time does the club open on Friday?","o":["6:00 a.m.","2:00 p.m.","11:00 p.m.","midnight"],"k":1,"e":"[detail] Friday: 2:00 p.m. – 11:00 p.m.","h":"سطر Friday."},{"n":17,"s":"On which day is the club open until midnight?","o":["Thursday","Friday","Saturday","Monday"],"k":0,"e":"[detail] Thursday: 6:00 a.m. – midnight.","h":"الخميس."},{"n":18,"s":"When is the swimming pool closed?","o":["every Friday","every Thursday","every morning","every Monday"],"k":3,"e":"[detail] closed every Monday for cleaning.","h":"يوم الاثنين."},{"n":19,"s":"How much does the football field cost?","o":["100 riyals a day","free for one week","100 riyals an hour","1,000 riyals a month"],"k":2,"e":"[detail] 100 riyals an hour.","h":"مئة ريال للساعة."},{"n":20,"s":"What is this text mainly about?","o":["the opening times and services of a sports club","how to play football","how to clean a swimming pool","the price of a gym bag"],"k":0,"e":"[main idea] The whole notice gives the club's hours and services.","h":"النص عن مواعيد النادي وخدماته."}]},{"l":["Text 5 (Questions 21–25): A class list with students' ages","(75 words)","Class 5A — Student List","1. Abdullah Al-Harbi — 10 years old — bus 3","2. Badr Al-Qahtani — 11 years old — walks","3. Fahad Al-Otaibi — 10 years old — bus 7","4. Hamza Al-Ghamdi — 11 years old — car","5. Mansour Al-Shehri — 12 years old — bus 3","6. Yousef Al-Zahrani — 10 years old — walks","Class teacher: Mr. Turki · Room 21","School starts at 7:00 a.m. Students who come by bus must wait at the main gate after school."],"q":[{"n":21,"s":"How old is Mansour?","o":["10","12","11","13"],"k":1,"e":"[detail] Mansour Al-Shehri — 12 years old.","h":"سطر منصور."},{"n":22,"s":"Which two students take bus 3?","o":["Fahad and Yousef","Badr and Hamza","Abdullah and Fahad","Abdullah and Mansour"],"k":3,"e":"[detail] Abdullah — bus 3; Mansour — bus 3.","h":"ابحث عن bus 3."},{"n":23,"s":"How does Hamza go to school?","o":["by bus","on foot","by bike","by car"],"k":3,"e":"[detail] Hamza Al-Ghamdi — car.","h":"بالسيارة."},{"n":24,"s":"Who is the class teacher?","o":["Mr. Mansour","Mr. Turki","Mr. Badr","Mr. Fahad"],"k":1,"e":"[detail] Class teacher: Mr. Turki.","h":"المعلم تركي."},{"n":25,"s":"How many students walk to school?","o":["two","one","three","four"],"k":0,"e":"[detail] Badr and Yousef walk.","h":"طالبان يمشيان."}]},{"l":["Text 6 (Questions 26–30): A flight information screen at the airport","(63 words)","King Khalid International Airport — Departures","SV 1020 to Jeddah 10:05 Gate 22 On time","SV 1214 to Abha 10:40 Gate 18 Delayed — new time 11:30","XY 405 to Dammam 11:15 Gate 9 Boarding","SV 563 to Cairo 12:00 Gate 31 On time","SV 789 to Madinah 12:45 Gate 22 Cancelled","Please check the screens for gate changes."],"q":[{"n":26,"s":"Which gate is the flight to Cairo?","o":["Gate 31","Gate 22","Gate 9","Gate 18"],"k":0,"e":"[detail] SV 563 to Cairo … Gate 31.","h":"سطر Cairo."},{"n":27,"s":"What is the new time of the flight to Abha?","o":["10:40","11:30","11:15","10:05"],"k":1,"e":"[detail] Delayed — new time 11:30.","h":"الوقت الجديد."},{"n":28,"s":"Which flight is cancelled?","o":["the flight to Jeddah","the flight to Dammam","the flight to Madinah","the flight to Cairo"],"k":2,"e":"[detail] SV 789 to Madinah … Cancelled.","h":"رحلة المدينة."},{"n":29,"s":"Passengers to which city are boarding now?","o":["Abha","Cairo","Dammam","Jeddah"],"k":2,"e":"[detail] XY 405 to Dammam … Boarding.","h":"Boarding = الصعود."},{"n":30,"s":"What is the purpose of this screen?","o":["to sell tickets to Cairo","to explain why flights are late","to show the weather in Riyadh","to give passengers information about flights"],"k":3,"e":"[purpose] A departures screen informs passengers about their flights.","h":"الغرض إعطاء معلومات عن الرحلات."}]}],"n":30},{"id":"1.3","t":"Words in Context (Simple Clues)","html":"<p><strong>Unit 1 · Lesson 1.3 · CEFR A1 · STEP link: Reading Comprehension (40%)</strong></p>\n<h3>Objectives</h3>\n<p>1. Guess the meaning of a new word from simple clues (examples, opposites, descriptions).</p>\n<p>2. Choose the option closest in meaning to a word in the text.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الأهداف</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">١. أن يخمّن الطالب معنى كلمة جديدة من القرائن البسيطة في النص مثل الأمثلة والأضداد والأوصاف.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٢. أن يختار البديل الأقرب في المعنى إلى كلمة في النص.</span></p>\n<h3>The Skill</h3>\n<p>STEP often asks about a word in the text. You may not know the word, but the sentences around it give clues.</p>\n<p>Clues can be an example (fruit such as apples), an opposite (not noisy but quiet), a description (He was tired; he slept for ten hours) or the result of an action.</p>\n<p><strong>Typical STEP question stems:</strong></p>\n<p>▸ The word … in the text is closest in meaning to …</p>\n<p>▸ What does the word … mean?</p>\n<p>▸ The word … could best be replaced by …</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">المهارة</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">يسأل اختبار STEP كثيرًا عن معنى كلمة في النص، وقد لا تعرف الكلمة، لكن الجمل المحيطة بها تعطيك قرائن مثل المثال أو الضد أو الوصف أو نتيجة الحدث.</span></p>\n<h3>Strategy</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>1. Find the word in the text and read the whole sentence.</p>\n<p>2. Read the sentence before and the sentence after.</p>\n<p>3. Look for a clue: an example, an opposite (but, not), or a description.</p>\n<p>4. Put each option in place of the word and read the sentence again.</p>\n<p>5. Choose the option that keeps the meaning of the sentence.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">ابحث عن الكلمة في النص واقرأ جملتها والجملة السابقة واللاحقة، وابحث عن قرينة، ثم ضع كل بديل مكان الكلمة واختر الذي يحافظ على معنى الجملة.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Traps and Distractor Types</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>✗ An option that looks like the word but means something different.</p>\n<p>✗ The usual dictionary meaning that does not fit this sentence.</p>\n<p>✗ An option that is the opposite of the clue.</p>\n<p>✗ An option that is true in the text but is not the meaning of the word.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Worked Example (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>Example text: A Busy Morning</strong></p>\n<p><em>(47 words)</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>The market was very crowded on Thursday morning. There were hundreds of people, and it was hard to walk. My father bought fresh fish, and my mother bought vegetables. By eleven o'clock, we were exhausted, so we sat down in a café and had a cold drink.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Example 1. The word crowded is closest in meaning to …</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. empty B. full of people C. clean D. expensive</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Clue: There were hundreds of people, and it was hard to walk.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Hundreds of people = full of people.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The answer is B.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Example 2. The word exhausted is closest in meaning to …</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. very tired B. very happy C. hungry D. late</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Clue: they sat down after a long time walking.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Sitting down after hard work shows they were very tired.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The answer is A.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">ابحث عن القرينة في الجملة التالية: مئات الناس تعني مزدحمًا، والجلوس بعد التعب يعني منهكًا.</span></p>","wu":"Worked example: Example 1 B · Example 2 A","quiz":[{"l":["Read each text and answer the questions. Choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","اقرأ كل نص ثم أجب عن الأسئلة التي تليه، واختر الإجابة الصحيحة من بين البدائل الأربعة.","Text 1 (Questions 1–5): A rainy day in Abha","(64 words)","Yesterday it rained in Abha all day. The streets were wet, and the air was cool. People stayed at home and drank hot tea with their families. In the evening, the rain stopped, and the sky became clear. We could see many stars. My little sister was thrilled. She jumped up and down and shouted, \"Look at the stars!\" It was a lovely evening."],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"The word cool is closest in meaning to …","o":["a little cold","very hot","dry","dirty"],"k":0,"e":"[vocabulary in context] Rain and wet streets suggest a little cold air.","h":"المطر يجعل الجو باردًا قليلًا."},{"n":2,"s":"The word clear is closest in meaning to …","o":["without clouds","dark","full of rain","very windy"],"k":0,"e":"[vocabulary in context] After the rain stopped, they could see stars — no clouds.","h":"رؤية النجوم تعني سماء صافية."},{"n":3,"s":"The word thrilled is closest in meaning to …","o":["very sad","very excited","very sleepy","afraid"],"k":1,"e":"[vocabulary in context] She jumped up and down and shouted — very excited.","h":"القفز والصراخ فرحًا."},{"n":4,"s":"What is the text mainly about?","o":["how to see stars","a trip to the market","my sister's school","a rainy day and a beautiful evening in Abha"],"k":3,"e":"[main idea] The whole text describes the day and evening in Abha.","h":"النص عن يوم ممطر وأمسية جميلة."},{"n":5,"s":"The word lovely is closest in meaning to …","o":["very long","very nice","very cold","very late"],"k":1,"e":"[vocabulary in context] The evening had stars and a happy girl — very nice.","h":"lovely تعني جميل."}]},{"l":["Text 2 (Questions 6–10): A very tall giraffe at the zoo","(69 words)","At Riyadh Zoo, the giraffe is the tallest animal. Her name is Lulu. Lulu has a very long neck, so she can reach the leaves at the top of the trees. Children love to watch her. Lulu is gentle; she never hurts other animals. Every day, a zookeeper gives her fresh leaves and fruit. She is five metres tall and weighs about 800 kilograms. Lulu chews her food slowly."],"q":[{"n":6,"s":"The word reach is closest in meaning to …","o":["cut","plant","count","get to"],"k":3,"e":"[vocabulary in context] Her long neck helps her get to the high leaves.","h":"الرقبة الطويلة تساعدها على الوصول."},{"n":7,"s":"The word gentle is closest in meaning to …","o":["kind and calm","fast","angry","noisy"],"k":0,"e":"[vocabulary in context] Clue: she never hurts other animals.","h":"القرينة: لا تؤذي أحدًا."},{"n":8,"s":"A zookeeper is a person who …","o":["sells tickets","builds trees","visits the zoo once","looks after animals in a zoo"],"k":3,"e":"[vocabulary in context] The zookeeper gives her leaves and fruit every day.","h":"يعتني بالحيوانات."},{"n":9,"s":"The word chews is closest in meaning to …","o":["throws away","eats slowly with her teeth","smells","washes"],"k":1,"e":"[vocabulary in context] She chews her food slowly — uses her teeth.","h":"يمضغ الطعام."},{"n":10,"s":"Why can Lulu eat leaves at the top of trees?","o":["She can climb trees.","The trees are very short.","She has a very long neck.","The zookeeper cuts them."],"k":2,"e":"[cause–effect] so she can reach the leaves → because of her long neck.","h":"بسبب رقبتها الطويلة."}]},{"l":["Text 3 (Questions 11–15): Making a cheese sandwich for lunch","(71 words)","Making a cheese sandwich is simple. First, take two slices of bread. Spread a little butter on each slice. Then put a thick piece of cheese on one slice. You can add a few slices of tomato. Put the second slice on top and press it gently. Cut the sandwich in half. Put it on a clean plate and pour a glass of cold milk. It is quick, easy and delicious!"],"q":[{"n":11,"s":"The word simple is closest in meaning to …","o":["easy","expensive","difficult","slow"],"k":0,"e":"[vocabulary in context] Clue: the last sentence says quick, easy and delicious.","h":"simple = easy."},{"n":12,"s":"The word slices is closest in meaning to …","o":["big bags","cups","bottles","thin pieces"],"k":3,"e":"[vocabulary in context] two slices of bread → thin pieces of bread.","h":"شرائح."},{"n":13,"s":"The word thick is the opposite of …","o":["soft","fresh","thin","cold"],"k":2,"e":"[vocabulary in context] A thick piece is the opposite of a thin one.","h":"عكس thick هو thin."},{"n":14,"s":"The word delicious is closest in meaning to …","o":["very hot","very tasty","very big","very old"],"k":1,"e":"[vocabulary in context] We use delicious to describe good food.","h":"لذيذ."},{"n":15,"s":"What do you do after you put the second slice on top?","o":["add tomato","spread butter","press it gently","take two slices of bread"],"k":2,"e":"[sequence] Put the second slice on top and press it gently.","h":"الترتيب في النص."}]},{"l":["Text 4 (Questions 16–20): A noisy classroom on Monday","(66 words)","On Monday, our classroom was very noisy. The students were talking and laughing, and nobody listened to the teacher. Some students were throwing paper balls, and others were walking around the room. Mr. Hamad was annoyed. He stopped the lesson and said, \"Please be quiet.\" Suddenly, the room was silent. Everyone sat down and opened their books. Then Mr. Hamad smiled and started the lesson again."],"q":[{"n":16,"s":"The word noisy is closest in meaning to …","o":["very clean","very cold","full of loud sounds","empty"],"k":2,"e":"[vocabulary in context] Students were talking and laughing — loud sounds.","h":"أصوات عالية."},{"n":17,"s":"The word annoyed is closest in meaning to …","o":["very happy","a little angry","very tired","surprised and pleased"],"k":1,"e":"[vocabulary in context] Nobody listened, so he stopped the lesson — a little angry.","h":"منزعج."},{"n":18,"s":"The word silent is the opposite of …","o":["empty","dark","hot","noisy"],"k":3,"e":"[vocabulary in context] After be quiet, the room was silent — no noise.","h":"عكس صامت."},{"n":19,"s":"The word Suddenly is closest in meaning to …","o":["slowly","every day","very quickly and without warning","later"],"k":2,"e":"[vocabulary in context] The room changed at once.","h":"فجأة."},{"n":20,"s":"What did Mr. Hamad do first?","o":["He stopped the lesson.","He smiled.","He started laughing.","He left the room."],"k":0,"e":"[sequence] He stopped the lesson and said, Please be quiet.","h":"أوقف الدرس أولًا."}]},{"l":["Text 5 (Questions 21–25): A tired football player after a match","(66 words)","Ali plays football for his school team. Last Thursday, they had a big match. Ali ran for ninety minutes and scored two goals. After the match, he was worn out. He could not walk fast, and his legs hurt. His mother made him a big bowl of soup. He went home, had a shower and slept for ten hours. The next morning, he felt strong again."],"q":[{"n":21,"s":"The phrase worn out is closest in meaning to …","o":["very tired","very angry","very proud","very hungry"],"k":0,"e":"[vocabulary in context] Clue: he could not walk fast and slept for ten hours.","h":"منهك جدًا."},{"n":22,"s":"The word scored is closest in meaning to …","o":["missed","watched","lost","got (points or goals)"],"k":3,"e":"[vocabulary in context] scored two goals = got two goals.","h":"سجّل."},{"n":23,"s":"The word strong is the opposite of …","o":["weak","fast","happy","young"],"k":0,"e":"[vocabulary in context] He felt strong again after resting.","h":"عكس قوي ضعيف."},{"n":24,"s":"How long did Ali sleep?","o":["two hours","ten hours","ninety minutes","all day"],"k":1,"e":"[detail] slept for ten hours.","h":"عشر ساعات."},{"n":25,"s":"What is the text mostly about?","o":["how to score goals","Ali's big match and how tired he was after it","Ali's school bus","a football shop"],"k":1,"e":"[main idea] The text tells about the match and its effect on Ali.","h":"المباراة وتعب علي."}]},{"l":["Text 6 (Questions 26–30): A small spice shop in the old souq","(69 words)","In the old souq in Jeddah, there is a small spice shop. It is narrow, but it is full of colours and smells. There are big bags of cumin, cardamom and black pepper. The owner, Uncle Saleh, is very friendly. He gives every customer a free cup of coffee. His grandfather opened the shop more than fifty years ago. Many tourists visit his shop, and they always buy something."],"q":[{"n":26,"s":"The word narrow is closest in meaning to …","o":["not wide","very old","very dark","very tall"],"k":0,"e":"[vocabulary in context] It is narrow, but it is full — a small, not wide shop.","h":"ضيق."},{"n":27,"s":"The word owner is closest in meaning to …","o":["a visitor","a driver","the person the shop belongs to","a cook"],"k":2,"e":"[vocabulary in context] Uncle Saleh owns the shop.","h":"صاحب المحل."},{"n":28,"s":"The word friendly is closest in meaning to …","o":["shy","rich","busy","kind and nice to people"],"k":3,"e":"[vocabulary in context] Clue: he gives every customer free coffee.","h":"ودود."},{"n":29,"s":"A customer is a person who …","o":["works in a shop","cleans a shop","buys something from a shop","builds a shop"],"k":2,"e":"[vocabulary in context] Customers buy things.","h":"الزبون."},{"n":30,"s":"What does Uncle Saleh give every customer?","o":["a bag of pepper","a map of Jeddah","a discount card","a free cup of coffee"],"k":3,"e":"[detail] He gives every customer a free cup of coffee.","h":"فنجان قهوة مجاني."}]}],"n":30},{"id":"1.4","t":"Reference Words (he, she, it, they, this)","html":"<p><strong>Unit 1 · Lesson 1.4 · CEFR A1 · STEP link: Reading Comprehension (40%)</strong></p>\n<h3>Objectives</h3>\n<p>1. Find what he, she, it, they and this refer to.</p>\n<p>2. Track simple references across two or three sentences.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الأهداف</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">١. أن يحدد الطالب ما تعود عليه الضمائر he وshe وit وthey وthis.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٢. أن يتتبع الإحالة عبر جملتين أو ثلاث.</span></p>\n<h3>The Skill</h3>\n<p>Writers use small words like he, she, it, they, them, his and this so they do not repeat the same noun again and again. These are reference words.</p>\n<p>To understand a text, you must know what each reference word points back to. STEP often asks: The word 'it' in line 3 refers to … In this booklet, the texts are not printed in fixed lines, so we count sentences instead.</p>\n<p><strong>Typical STEP question stems:</strong></p>\n<p>▸ The word 'they' in the text refers to …</p>\n<p>▸ What does 'it' refer to?</p>\n<p>▸ Who does 'she' refer to?</p>\n<p>▸ The word 'this' refers to …</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">المهارة</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">يستخدم الكاتب كلمات صغيرة مثل he وshe وit وthey وthis حتى لا يكرر الاسم نفسه، وتسمى كلمات الإحالة، ولفهم النص يجب أن تعرف الاسم الذي تعود عليه كل كلمة.</span></p>\n<h3>Strategy</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>1. Find the reference word in the text.</p>\n<p>2. Look BACK at the sentences before it.</p>\n<p>3. Check number: he / she / it = one; they / them = more than one.</p>\n<p>4. Check type: he / she = a person; it = a thing or animal.</p>\n<p>5. Put your answer in place of the word and read the sentence again.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">ابحث عن كلمة الإحالة، ثم ارجع إلى الجمل السابقة، وتحقق من العدد (مفرد أم جمع) ومن النوع (شخص أم شيء)، ثم ضع إجابتك مكان الكلمة واقرأ الجملة.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Traps and Distractor Types</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>✗ The nearest noun is not always the right answer.</p>\n<p>✗ A plural word (they) cannot refer to one person.</p>\n<p>✗ it usually refers to a thing or an animal, not a person.</p>\n<p>✗ this can refer to a whole idea, not only a noun.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Worked Example (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>Example text: The Lost Wallet</strong></p>\n<p><em>(42 words)</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Omar found a wallet on the bus. It was brown and full of cards. He gave it to the driver. The driver called the owner, a young man named Yasser. He was very happy and thanked Omar. This made Omar feel proud.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Example 1. The word 'It' in sentence 2 refers to …</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. the bus B. the wallet C. the driver D. the card</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Look back: Omar found a wallet on the bus.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> It was brown and full of cards — a wallet is full of cards, not a bus.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The answer is B.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Example 2. The word 'This' in the last sentence refers to …</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. the bus ride B. Yasser thanking Omar</p>\n<p>C. the brown colour D. the cards</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> This refers to the idea before it.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Yasser was happy and thanked Omar — this made Omar proud.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The answer is B.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">ارجع إلى الجمل السابقة وطابق العدد والنوع، وتذكّر أن this قد تعود على فكرة كاملة.</span></p>","wu":"Worked example: Example 1 B · Example 2 B","quiz":[{"l":["Read each text and answer the questions. Choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","اقرأ كل نص ثم أجب عن الأسئلة التي تليه، واختر الإجابة الصحيحة من بين البدائل الأربعة.","Text 1 (Questions 1–5): Two brothers and their bicycles","(66 words)","Saad and Majed are brothers. They each have a bicycle. Saad's bicycle is red, and Majed's is blue. Every afternoon, they ride them to the park near their house. Yesterday, Majed's bicycle had a flat tyre. Saad helped him fix it. Then the brothers rode together again. Their mother says they are good friends as well as brothers. On Fridays, the whole family goes cycling together."],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"The word 'They' in sentence 2 refers to …","o":["the bicycles","their parents","Saad and Majed","the parks"],"k":2,"e":"[reference] They each have a bicycle → the two brothers.","h":"they تعود على الأخوين."},{"n":2,"s":"The word 'them' in sentence 4 refers to …","o":["the brothers","the bicycles","the houses","the parks"],"k":1,"e":"[reference] They ride them → they ride the bicycles.","h":"them تعود على الدراجات."},{"n":3,"s":"The word 'him' in sentence 6 refers to …","o":["Saad","Majed","their father","the tyre"],"k":1,"e":"[reference] Majed's bicycle had a flat tyre. Saad helped him.","h":"him تعود على ماجد."},{"n":4,"s":"The word 'it' in sentence 6 refers to …","o":["the park","the house","Saad's bicycle","the flat tyre"],"k":3,"e":"[reference] Saad helped him fix it — the flat tyre.","h":"it تعود على الإطار."},{"n":5,"s":"What is the main idea of the text?","o":["Red bicycles are better than blue ones.","Two brothers ride bicycles and help each other.","The park is near the house.","Flat tyres are a big problem."],"k":1,"e":"[main idea] The text is about the brothers and their friendship.","h":"الفكرة عن الأخوين وتعاونهما."}]},{"l":["Text 2 (Questions 6–10): A teacher and her new students","(67 words)","Ms. Sarah is a new English teacher at our school. She came from Canada last month. On the first day, she was nervous, but the students were very kind to her. They made a welcome card, and she put it on the classroom wall. Now she knows all their names. She says they are the best class in the school. Her students are proud of her too."],"q":[{"n":6,"s":"The word 'She' in sentence 2 refers to …","o":["the school","a student","the welcome card","Ms. Sarah"],"k":3,"e":"[reference] She came from Canada → Ms. Sarah.","h":"she تعود على المعلمة سارة."},{"n":7,"s":"The word 'her' in sentence 3 refers to …","o":["the card","a student's mother","Ms. Sarah","Canada"],"k":2,"e":"[reference] the students were very kind to her → the teacher.","h":"her تعود على المعلمة."},{"n":8,"s":"The word 'it' in sentence 4 refers to …","o":["the classroom","the welcome card","the school","the first day"],"k":1,"e":"[reference] she put it on the classroom wall → the card.","h":"it تعود على البطاقة."},{"n":9,"s":"The word 'their' in sentence 5 refers to …","o":["the teachers'","the parents'","the students'","the walls'"],"k":2,"e":"[reference] she knows all their names → the students' names.","h":"their تعود على الطلاب."},{"n":10,"s":"How did Ms. Sarah feel on the first day?","o":["nervous","angry","bored","sleepy"],"k":0,"e":"[detail] On the first day, she was nervous.","h":"كانت متوترة."}]},{"l":["Text 3 (Questions 11–15): A dog that helps a farmer","(67 words)","Mr. Abdulrahman has a farm with many sheep. He also has a big brown dog called Rocky. Rocky helps him every day. In the morning, it takes the sheep to the field. In the evening, it brings them back. Rocky is very clever; it never loses a sheep. Rocky also guards the farm at night and barks at strangers. Mr. Abdulrahman says, \"He is my best worker!\""],"q":[{"n":11,"s":"The word 'him' in sentence 3 refers to …","o":["Mr. Abdulrahman","Rocky","a sheep","the field"],"k":0,"e":"[reference] Rocky helps him → the farmer.","h":"him تعود على المزارع."},{"n":12,"s":"The word 'it' in sentence 4 refers to …","o":["the farm","Rocky","the morning","the field"],"k":1,"e":"[reference] it takes the sheep to the field → the dog.","h":"it تعود على الكلب."},{"n":13,"s":"The word 'them' in sentence 5 refers to …","o":["the dogs","the fields","the workers","the sheep"],"k":3,"e":"[reference] it brings them back → the sheep.","h":"them تعود على الأغنام."},{"n":14,"s":"In the last sentence, 'He' refers to …","o":["Rocky","Mr. Abdulrahman","a worker","a sheep"],"k":0,"e":"[reference] He is my best worker — the farmer is talking about Rocky.","h":"He هنا تعود على روكي."},{"n":15,"s":"Why does the farmer like Rocky?","o":["Rocky helps him and never loses a sheep.","Rocky is big and brown.","Rocky sleeps all day.","Rocky eats very little."],"k":0,"e":"[cause–effect] Rocky helps every day and never loses a sheep.","h":"لأنه يساعده ولا يضيع الأغنام."}]},{"l":["Text 4 (Questions 16–20): A girl and her favourite storybook","(67 words)","Nour is eight years old. Her favourite book is about a little falcon that learns to fly. She reads it every night before she sleeps. Her father bought it for her at a book fair in Riyadh. The pictures in it are bright and beautiful. She has read it more than twenty times. Nour's friends want to borrow it, but she says, \"This book is my treasure!\""],"q":[{"n":16,"s":"The word 'Her' in sentence 2 refers to …","o":["the falcon's","Nour's","her father's","her friend's"],"k":1,"e":"[reference] Her favourite book → Nour's book.","h":"her تعود على نور."},{"n":17,"s":"The word 'it' in sentence 3 refers to …","o":["the falcon","the night","the bed","the book"],"k":3,"e":"[reference] She reads it every night → the book.","h":"it تعود على الكتاب."},{"n":18,"s":"In 'Her father bought it for her', the word 'her' refers to …","o":["the falcon","a teacher","Nour","the book fair"],"k":2,"e":"[reference] Her father bought it for her → Nour.","h":"her تعود على نور."},{"n":19,"s":"In 'The pictures in it are bright', the word 'it' refers to …","o":["the book fair","the book","Riyadh","the picture"],"k":1,"e":"[reference] The pictures in it → in the book.","h":"in it = in the book."},{"n":20,"s":"What is the book about?","o":["a girl who goes to Riyadh","a book fair","a little falcon that learns to fly","a beautiful treasure"],"k":2,"e":"[detail] Her favourite book is about a little falcon that learns to fly.","h":"عن صقر صغير."}]},{"l":["Text 5 (Questions 21–25): A family's new car","(70 words)","Last month, my family bought a new car. It is white and has seven seats. My father chose it because our family is big. My mother likes it because it is safe and comfortable. On Friday, we drove it to Al-Ula. The trip was long, but nobody was tired. My little brothers slept, and my sisters played word games. We arrived in the evening and stayed at a small hotel."],"q":[{"n":21,"s":"The word 'It' in sentence 2 refers to …","o":["the family","the month","the seat","the new car"],"k":3,"e":"[reference] It is white and has seven seats → the car.","h":"it تعود على السيارة."},{"n":22,"s":"Why did the father choose this car?","o":["because it is cheap","because it is fast","because the family is big","because it is white"],"k":2,"e":"[cause–effect] My father chose it because our family is big.","h":"لأن العائلة كبيرة."},{"n":23,"s":"In 'My mother likes it', the word 'it' refers to …","o":["the car","the safety","the mother","the trip"],"k":0,"e":"[reference] My mother likes it → the car.","h":"it تعود على السيارة."},{"n":24,"s":"Where did the family drive on Friday?","o":["to Al-Ula","to Riyadh","to the car shop","to school"],"k":0,"e":"[detail] we drove it to Al-Ula.","h":"إلى العلا."},{"n":25,"s":"What did the writer's sisters do during the trip?","o":["They slept.","They drove the car.","They felt tired.","They played word games."],"k":3,"e":"[detail] my sisters played word games.","h":"لعبن ألعاب الكلمات."}]},{"l":["Text 6 (Questions 26–30): Friends who play basketball after school","(65 words)","Every day after school, Hassan, Adel and Ibrahim play basketball in the school yard. They practise for one hour. Their coach, Mr. Yasser, watches them and gives them advice. He says Adel is the best shooter in the team. This makes Adel very happy. Next month, they will play in a city competition. The boys are training hard because they want to win the cup."],"q":[{"n":26,"s":"The word 'They' in sentence 2 refers to …","o":["Hassan, Adel and Ibrahim","the teachers","the coaches","the parents"],"k":0,"e":"[reference] They practise for one hour → the three boys.","h":"they تعود على الأولاد الثلاثة."},{"n":27,"s":"The word 'He' in sentence 4 refers to …","o":["Adel","Hassan","Mr. Yasser","Ibrahim"],"k":2,"e":"[reference] He says Adel is the best shooter → the coach.","h":"He تعود على المدرب."},{"n":28,"s":"The word 'This' in sentence 5 refers to …","o":["the school yard","the coach saying that Adel is the best shooter","the basketball","the city competition"],"k":1,"e":"[reference] This makes Adel very happy → the coach's words.","h":"This تعود على كلام المدرب."},{"n":29,"s":"How long do the boys practise?","o":["two hours","thirty minutes","one hour","all afternoon"],"k":2,"e":"[detail] They practise for one hour.","h":"ساعة واحدة."},{"n":30,"s":"Which is the best title?","o":["The Best Shooter in the City","A City Competition","Mr. Yasser's Car","Three Friends and Their Basketball Practice"],"k":3,"e":"[best title] The text is about the boys practising.","h":"عنوان شامل."}]}],"n":30},{"id":"1.5","t":"Detail Questions","html":"<p><strong>Unit 1 · Lesson 1.5 · CEFR A1 · STEP link: Reading Comprehension (40%)</strong></p>\n<h3>Objectives</h3>\n<p>1. Locate the sentence that answers a detail question.</p>\n<p>2. Match simple paraphrased options to words in the text.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الأهداف</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">١. أن يحدد الطالب الجملة التي تجيب عن سؤال التفاصيل.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٢. أن يطابق البدائل المعاد صياغتها مع كلمات النص.</span></p>\n<h3>The Skill</h3>\n<p>Detail questions ask about one fact in the text: who, what, where, when, how many or why. The answer is written in the text, but often with different words.</p>\n<p>The correct option may paraphrase the text: bought a new pair of shoes may become got new shoes.</p>\n<p><strong>Typical STEP question stems:</strong></p>\n<p>▸ According to the text, …</p>\n<p>▸ What did … do …?</p>\n<p>▸ Where / When / How many …?</p>\n<p>▸ Which of the following is TRUE?</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">المهارة</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">أسئلة التفاصيل تسأل عن معلومة واحدة في النص: من؟ ماذا؟ أين؟ متى؟ كم؟ لماذا؟ والإجابة موجودة في النص لكنها قد تأتي بكلمات مختلفة.</span></p>\n<h3>Strategy</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>1. Read the question and find its key word.</p>\n<p>2. Scan the text for the key word or a word with the same meaning.</p>\n<p>3. Read that sentence slowly.</p>\n<p>4. Compare each option with the sentence — look for the same MEANING, not the same words.</p>\n<p>5. Reject options that add information that is not in the text.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">حدّد الكلمة المفتاحية في السؤال، وابحث عنها أو عن مرادفها في النص، واقرأ الجملة ببطء، ثم قارن المعنى لا الكلمات، واستبعد البدائل التي تضيف معلومات غير موجودة.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Traps and Distractor Types</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>✗ Same words, different meaning: the option copies text words but changes the fact.</p>\n<p>✗ Right information, wrong person or time.</p>\n<p>✗ Information that is true in real life but not in the text.</p>\n<p>✗ Half-true options: one part is correct, the other is not.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Worked Example (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>Example text: A Trip to the Bookshop</strong></p>\n<p><em>(48 words)</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>On Saturday, Huda went to the bookshop with her aunt. She wanted a new English dictionary. The shop had three kinds, and she chose the small blue one because it fits in her school bag. Her aunt paid forty riyals for it and also bought Huda a notebook.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Example 1. Why did Huda choose the blue dictionary?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. It was cheap. B. It was small enough for her bag.</p>\n<p>C. Her aunt liked blue. D. It was the only one.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Key word: Why … choose.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Text: she chose the small blue one because it fits in her school bag.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Paraphrase: small enough for her bag. The answer is B.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Example 2. Which of the following is TRUE?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. Huda paid forty riyals.</p>\n<p>B. Huda went alone.</p>\n<p>C. Huda's aunt bought her a notebook.</p>\n<p>D. The shop had one kind of dictionary.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Check each option.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> A: the aunt paid; B: she went with her aunt; D: three kinds.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> C matches the last sentence. The answer is C.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">ابحث عن الجملة التي تحتوي الإجابة، ثم طابق المعنى، واحذر البدائل التي تغيّر الشخص أو العدد.</span></p>","wu":"Worked example: Example 1 B · Example 2 C","quiz":[{"l":["Read each text and answer the questions. Choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","اقرأ كل نص ثم أجب عن الأسئلة التي تليه، واختر الإجابة الصحيحة من بين البدائل الأربعة.","Text 1 (Questions 1–5): A visit to the dentist","(64 words)","Yesterday I went to the dentist with my father. The dentist, Dr. Mona, was very kind. She looked at my teeth with a small mirror. She said I had one small hole in a back tooth. She cleaned it and filled it in ten minutes. It did not hurt. Dr. Mona told me to brush my teeth twice a day and eat fewer sweets."],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"Who went to the dentist with the writer?","o":["the writer's father","the writer's mother","Dr. Mona","a friend"],"k":0,"e":"[detail] I went to the dentist with my father.","h":"مع والده."},{"n":2,"s":"What did the dentist find?","o":["two broken teeth","a small hole in a back tooth","a problem with the mirror","nothing wrong"],"k":1,"e":"[detail] one small hole in a back tooth.","h":"تسوس صغير."},{"n":3,"s":"How long did the treatment take?","o":["one hour","ten minutes","two days","twenty minutes"],"k":1,"e":"[detail] filled it in ten minutes.","h":"عشر دقائق."},{"n":4,"s":"According to the text, the treatment …","o":["was not painful","was very painful","was expensive","took all day"],"k":0,"e":"[detail] It did not hurt = not painful.","h":"لم يؤلمه."},{"n":5,"s":"What advice did Dr. Mona give?","o":["visit her every week","never eat sweets again","use a small mirror","brush twice a day and eat fewer sweets"],"k":3,"e":"[detail] brush my teeth twice a day and eat fewer sweets.","h":"النصيحة."}]},{"l":["Text 2 (Questions 6–10): Shopping for new school shoes","(62 words)","Last week, I needed new school shoes because my old ones were too small. My mother and I went to a shoe shop in the mall. I tried on four pairs. The black ones were comfortable, but they were too expensive. Finally, I chose a pair of dark blue shoes. They cost 120 riyals. My mother also bought me some white socks."],"q":[{"n":6,"s":"Why did the writer need new shoes?","o":["The old shoes were broken.","The old shoes were dirty.","The old shoes were the wrong colour.","The old shoes were too small."],"k":3,"e":"[cause–effect] my old ones were too small.","h":"الحذاء القديم صغير."},{"n":7,"s":"How many pairs did the writer try on?","o":["four","two","three","one"],"k":0,"e":"[detail] I tried on four pairs.","h":"أربعة أزواج."},{"n":8,"s":"What was the problem with the black shoes?","o":["They were too small.","They cost too much.","They were not comfortable.","They were the wrong size."],"k":1,"e":"[detail] too expensive = cost too much.","h":"غالية الثمن."},{"n":9,"s":"What colour were the shoes the writer bought?","o":["black","white","brown","dark blue"],"k":3,"e":"[detail] I chose a pair of dark blue shoes.","h":"أزرق داكن."},{"n":10,"s":"Which of the following is TRUE?","o":["The new shoes cost 200 riyals.","The writer went to the shop alone.","The writer's mother bought socks too.","The writer bought the black shoes."],"k":2,"e":"[detail] My mother also bought me some white socks.","h":"اشترت الجوارب."}]},{"l":["Text 3 (Questions 11–15): A weekend at the beach in Yanbu","(61 words)","Last summer, my family spent a weekend at the beach in Yanbu. The water was clear and warm. My brothers swam every morning, and I collected shells. In the afternoons, we sat under a big umbrella because the sun was very strong. In the evenings, we had grilled fish at a small restaurant. It was the best weekend of the summer."],"q":[{"n":11,"s":"When did the brothers swim?","o":["every morning","every afternoon","every evening","only once"],"k":0,"e":"[detail] My brothers swam every morning.","h":"كل صباح."},{"n":12,"s":"What did the writer do at the beach?","o":["collected shells","went fishing","swam every morning","built a sandcastle"],"k":0,"e":"[detail] I collected shells.","h":"جمع الأصداف."},{"n":13,"s":"Why did they sit under an umbrella?","o":["It was raining.","It was very windy.","The water was cold.","The sun was very strong."],"k":3,"e":"[cause–effect] because the sun was very strong.","h":"بسبب الشمس القوية."},{"n":14,"s":"What did the family eat in the evenings?","o":["chicken and rice","grilled fish","pizza","sandwiches"],"k":1,"e":"[detail] we had grilled fish.","h":"سمك مشوي."},{"n":15,"s":"What does the writer think of the weekend?","o":["It was too hot.","It was boring.","It was the best weekend of the summer.","It was too short."],"k":2,"e":"[main idea] the best weekend of the summer.","h":"أفضل عطلة."}]},{"l":["Text 4 (Questions 16–20): A boy's pet goldfish","(73 words)","Ahmed has a pet goldfish called Sunny. Sunny lives in a round glass bowl on Ahmed's desk. Ahmed feeds him twice a day, once in the morning and once in the evening. Every Saturday, Ahmed cleans the bowl with his father's help. He gives Sunny only a little food, because too much food is bad for fish. Sunny is three years old. Ahmed likes to watch him swim while he does his homework."],"q":[{"n":16,"s":"Where does Sunny live?","o":["in a pond in the garden","in the kitchen","in a glass bowl on Ahmed's desk","in a big tank at school"],"k":2,"e":"[detail] a round glass bowl on Ahmed's desk.","h":"حوض زجاجي على المكتب."},{"n":17,"s":"How often does Ahmed feed Sunny?","o":["once a day","three times a day","every Saturday","twice a day"],"k":3,"e":"[detail] Ahmed feeds him twice a day.","h":"مرتين يوميًا."},{"n":18,"s":"Who helps Ahmed clean the bowl?","o":["his father","his mother","his brother","nobody"],"k":0,"e":"[detail] with his father's help.","h":"والده."},{"n":19,"s":"How old is Sunny?","o":["two","four","twelve","three"],"k":3,"e":"[detail] Sunny is three years old.","h":"ثلاث سنوات."},{"n":20,"s":"The word 'him' in the last sentence refers to …","o":["Sunny","Ahmed","Ahmed's father","the bowl"],"k":0,"e":"[reference] watch him swim → the fish.","h":"him تعود على السمكة."}]},{"l":["Text 5 (Questions 21–25): A new student from Egypt","(61 words)","A new student joined our class this week. His name is Karim, and he is from Cairo in Egypt. His father works as an engineer in Riyadh. Karim speaks Arabic and English very well. He likes football and drawing. On his first day, he sat next to me, and I showed him the library and the cafeteria. Now we are friends."],"q":[{"n":21,"s":"Where is Karim from?","o":["Riyadh","Cairo","Jeddah","London"],"k":1,"e":"[detail] he is from Cairo in Egypt.","h":"من القاهرة."},{"n":22,"s":"What is Karim's father's job?","o":["engineer","teacher","doctor","pilot"],"k":0,"e":"[detail] His father works as an engineer.","h":"مهندس."},{"n":23,"s":"Which languages does Karim speak well?","o":["only Arabic","English and French","Arabic and English","only English"],"k":2,"e":"[detail] Karim speaks Arabic and English very well.","h":"العربية والإنجليزية."},{"n":24,"s":"What did the writer show Karim?","o":["the gym and the garden","the library and the cafeteria","the office","his house"],"k":1,"e":"[detail] I showed him the library and the cafeteria.","h":"المكتبة والمقصف."},{"n":25,"s":"What is the text mainly about?","o":["a library in Riyadh","an engineer's job","a football team","a new classmate from Egypt"],"k":3,"e":"[main idea] The text describes the new student, Karim.","h":"عن زميل جديد."}]},{"l":["Text 6 (Questions 26–30): Cooking rice with Father","(62 words)","On Thursday evening, I cooked rice with my father for the first time. First, we washed two cups of rice. Then my father put some oil in a big pot and added chopped onions. After that, we added the rice and four cups of water. We waited for twenty minutes. The rice was soft and delicious. My mother said it was perfect!"],"q":[{"n":26,"s":"When did the writer cook rice?","o":["on Friday morning","on Thursday evening","on Thursday morning","every day"],"k":1,"e":"[detail] On Thursday evening.","h":"مساء الخميس."},{"n":27,"s":"How many cups of water did they add?","o":["two","three","four","twenty"],"k":2,"e":"[detail] four cups of water.","h":"أربعة أكواب."},{"n":28,"s":"What did the father put in the pot first?","o":["the rice","the water","some oil","the onions"],"k":2,"e":"[sequence] my father put some oil in a big pot and added chopped onions.","h":"الزيت أولًا."},{"n":29,"s":"How long did they wait?","o":["two minutes","twenty minutes","four minutes","an hour"],"k":1,"e":"[detail] We waited for twenty minutes.","h":"عشرون دقيقة."},{"n":30,"s":"What did the writer's mother think of the rice?","o":["It was too soft.","It needed more salt.","It was perfect.","It was burnt."],"k":2,"e":"[detail] My mother said it was perfect!","h":"قالت إنه ممتاز."}]}],"n":30},{"id":"1.6","t":"Real-life Texts: Signs, Notices, Messages and Short Emails","html":"<p><strong>Unit 1 · Lesson 1.6 · CEFR A1 · STEP link: Reading Comprehension (40%)</strong></p>\n<h3>Objectives</h3>\n<p>1. Understand the purpose of signs, notices, messages and short emails.</p>\n<p>2. Find practical information: time, place and the action needed.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الأهداف</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">١. أن يفهم الطالب الغرض من اللافتات والإعلانات والرسائل والبريد الإلكتروني القصير.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٢. أن يجد المعلومات العملية: الوقت والمكان والمطلوب فعله.</span></p>\n<h3>The Skill</h3>\n<p>Real-life texts are short and practical. They tell people what to do, what not to do, or what is happening.</p>\n<p>For these texts, ask three questions: Who wrote it? Who is it for? What must the reader do?</p>\n<p><strong>Typical STEP question stems:</strong></p>\n<p>▸ What does this sign mean?</p>\n<p>▸ Why did … write this message?</p>\n<p>▸ What should the reader do?</p>\n<p>▸ Where would you see this notice?</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">المهارة</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">النصوص الواقعية قصيرة وعملية، تخبر القارئ بما يجب أن يفعله أو بما لا يجب أن يفعله أو بما يحدث. واسأل دائمًا: من كتب النص؟ ولمن؟ وما المطلوب من القارئ؟</span></p>\n<h3>Strategy</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>1. Look at the type of text: sign, notice, message or email.</p>\n<p>2. Find who wrote it and who it is for.</p>\n<p>3. Find the action words (please, do not, must, call, bring).</p>\n<p>4. Look for times, dates and places.</p>\n<p>5. Choose the option that explains the purpose, not just repeats words.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">حدّد نوع النص، ثم الكاتب والقارئ، وابحث عن كلمات الفعل المطلوب مثل please وdo not وmust، ثم عن الأوقات والأماكن، واختر الغرض الحقيقي للنص.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Traps and Distractor Types</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>✗ An option that repeats words from the sign but changes the meaning (No Parking ≠ parking here is free).</p>\n<p>✗ The right place but the wrong action.</p>\n<p>✗ Confusing the writer with the reader.</p>\n<p>✗ Choosing a detail instead of the purpose.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Worked Example (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>Example text: A Sign at the Swimming Pool</strong></p>\n<p><em>(30 words)</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>SWIMMING POOL RULES</p>\n<p>Children under 10 must swim with an adult.</p>\n<p>No running near the pool.</p>\n<p>No food or drinks in the water.</p>\n<p>The pool closes at 9 p.m.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Example 1. What does this sign tell people?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. how to swim faster B. the rules for using the pool</p>\n<p>C. the price of the pool D. where to buy food</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The title says SWIMMING POOL RULES.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Every line is a rule.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The answer is B.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Example 2. A boy is eight years old. What must he do?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. swim with an adult B. swim alone</p>\n<p>C. leave at 8 p.m. D. bring a drink</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Find the rule about age.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Children under 10 must swim with an adult; eight is under ten.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The answer is A.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">اقرأ العنوان لتعرف الغرض، ثم طبّق القاعدة المناسبة على الحالة في السؤال.</span></p>","wu":"Worked example: Example 1 B · Example 2 A","quiz":[{"l":["Read each text and answer the questions. Choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","اقرأ كل نص ثم أجب عن الأسئلة التي تليه، واختر الإجابة الصحيحة من بين البدائل الأربعة.","Text 1 (Questions 1–5): A No Parking sign at a hospital","(67 words)","KING FAHD HOSPITAL","NO PARKING","This area is for ambulances only — 24 hours a day.","Visitors: please use Car Park B behind the main building.","Cars parked here will be removed.","Car Park B is free for the first hour.","Patient drop-off: two minutes only, at the Main Entrance.","Taxis can wait at Gate 3.","Hospital Security — Tel. 012 555 0199","Thank you for helping our patients."],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"Where would you see this sign?","o":["at a school","at an airport","at a mall","at a hospital"],"k":3,"e":"[purpose] The sign starts with KING FAHD HOSPITAL.","h":"عند المستشفى."},{"n":2,"s":"Who can stop in this area?","o":["visitors","taxis","ambulances","buses"],"k":2,"e":"[detail] This area is for ambulances only.","h":"سيارات الإسعاف فقط."},{"n":3,"s":"Where should visitors park?","o":["in Car Park B","in this area","in front of the main door","on the street"],"k":0,"e":"[detail] Visitors: please use Car Park B.","h":"الموقف B."},{"n":4,"s":"What will happen to cars parked here?","o":["They will be taken away.","They will get a free ticket.","They will be washed.","Nothing will happen."],"k":0,"e":"[detail] Cars parked here will be removed = taken away.","h":"ستُسحب السيارات."},{"n":5,"s":"What is the main purpose of the sign?","o":["to sell parking tickets","to welcome new patients","to keep the area free for emergencies","to show the way to the hospital"],"k":2,"e":"[purpose] The area must be free for ambulances.","h":"إبقاء المكان للطوارئ."}]},{"l":["Text 2 (Questions 6–10): A text message about a late school bus","(67 words)","From: Mum","To: Hamad","Hamad, the school bus is late today. The driver called. It will come at 7:20, not at 6:50. Stay inside and finish your breakfast. Don't wait outside in the cold. Take your jacket and your lunch box from the kitchen table. Remember, you have football practice after school, so take your sports bag too. See you at 2 o'clock. Love, Mum"],"q":[{"n":6,"s":"Why did Mum send this message?","o":["to tell Hamad the bus is late","to ask Hamad to cook breakfast","to say she is ill","to invite Hamad to lunch"],"k":0,"e":"[purpose] The main news: the school bus is late today.","h":"لتخبره بتأخر الحافلة."},{"n":7,"s":"What time will the bus come?","o":["6:50","2:00","7:20","7:00"],"k":2,"e":"[detail] It will come at 7:20, not at 6:50.","h":"الساعة 7:20."},{"n":8,"s":"Where should Hamad wait?","o":["outside the house","inside the house","at the bus stop","at school"],"k":1,"e":"[detail] Stay inside … Don't wait outside.","h":"داخل البيت."},{"n":9,"s":"What must Hamad take from the kitchen table?","o":["his books","his jacket and lunch box","the car keys","his phone"],"k":1,"e":"[detail] Take your jacket and your lunch box from the kitchen table.","h":"سترته وصندوق غدائه."},{"n":10,"s":"Who called Mum?","o":["the bus driver","the teacher","Hamad","a neighbour"],"k":0,"e":"[detail] The driver called.","h":"السائق."}]},{"l":["Text 3 (Questions 11–15): A short email about a lost jacket","(67 words)","Subject: Lost jacket","Dear Mr. Fahad,","I think I left my jacket in Room 9 after the English lesson on Tuesday. It is dark green with a white zip, and my name is inside. There is a small black notebook in the pocket too. Can you please check the room? I can come to your office at the morning break tomorrow.","Thank you,","Faisal Al-Mutairi, Class 6B"],"q":[{"n":11,"s":"Why did Faisal write this email?","o":["to say sorry for being late","to ask for help finding his jacket","to ask about the English test","to invite Mr. Fahad to his house"],"k":1,"e":"[purpose] He thinks he left his jacket and asks the teacher to check.","h":"ليطلب المساعدة."},{"n":12,"s":"Where does Faisal think the jacket is?","o":["in the office","in the gym","at home","in Room 9"],"k":3,"e":"[detail] I left my jacket in Room 9.","h":"الغرفة 9."},{"n":13,"s":"What colour is the jacket?","o":["white","dark blue","black","dark green"],"k":3,"e":"[detail] It is dark green with a white zip.","h":"أخضر داكن."},{"n":14,"s":"How can someone know it is Faisal's jacket?","o":["His name is inside it.","It has a big pocket.","It is very new.","It has a red zip."],"k":0,"e":"[detail] my name is inside.","h":"اسمه بالداخل."},{"n":15,"s":"When will Faisal go to Mr. Fahad's office?","o":["on Tuesday after English","after school today","next week","at the morning break tomorrow"],"k":3,"e":"[detail] I can come to your office at the morning break tomorrow.","h":"استراحة الغد."}]},{"l":["Text 4 (Questions 16–20): A notice: the school library closes early","(68 words)","NOTICE","The school library will close early this week.","Sunday to Wednesday: open 7:30 a.m. – 12:00 p.m.","Thursday: closed (new computers are coming).","Please return all borrowed books by Wednesday.","From next Sunday, the library will open as usual until 2:00 p.m.","Students can still read e-books on the school website at any time.","Thank you for your help.","— Mrs. Amal, Librarian"],"q":[{"n":16,"s":"What is the notice mainly about?","o":["new books in the library","how to borrow books","the library's short opening hours this week","a computer lesson"],"k":2,"e":"[main idea] The library will close early this week.","h":"ساعات الدوام المختصرة."},{"n":17,"s":"When does the library close from Sunday to Wednesday?","o":["at 2:00 p.m.","at 7:30 a.m.","at 12:00 p.m.","at 1:00 p.m."],"k":2,"e":"[detail] open 7:30 a.m. – 12:00 p.m.","h":"الساعة 12 ظهرًا."},{"n":18,"s":"Why is the library closed on Thursday?","o":["The librarian is ill.","New computers are coming.","It is a holiday.","The books are old."],"k":1,"e":"[cause–effect] Thursday: closed (new computers are coming).","h":"وصول حواسيب جديدة."},{"n":19,"s":"What must students do by Wednesday?","o":["borrow new books","buy computers","visit Mrs. Amal at home","return borrowed books"],"k":3,"e":"[detail] Please return all borrowed books by Wednesday.","h":"إعادة الكتب."},{"n":20,"s":"Who wrote the notice?","o":["a student","the computer company","the head teacher","the librarian"],"k":3,"e":"[detail] — Mrs. Amal, Librarian.","h":"أمينة المكتبة."}]},{"l":["Text 5 (Questions 21–25): A museum ticket and its rules","(69 words)","SAUDI NATIONAL MUSEUM — ONE ADULT TICKET","Date: 12 February · Time: 10:00 a.m.","Price: 20 riyals (students with ID: free)","Opening hours: Sunday – Thursday, 9:00 a.m. – 8:00 p.m.","Museum rules:","Children under 12 must stay with an adult.","Please do not touch the objects.","Photos are allowed, but no flash.","Bags must be left at the front desk.","Keep this ticket until you leave."],"q":[{"n":21,"s":"Who can enter the museum for free?","o":["all adults","everyone on 12 February","students with an ID card","people with big bags"],"k":2,"e":"[detail] students with ID: free.","h":"الطلاب بالبطاقة."},{"n":22,"s":"Which of these is allowed in the museum?","o":["touching the objects","taking photos without flash","carrying a big bag","using a flash"],"k":1,"e":"[detail] Photos are allowed, but no flash.","h":"التصوير بلا فلاش."},{"n":23,"s":"Where must visitors leave their bags?","o":["in the car","next to the objects","at home","at the front desk"],"k":3,"e":"[detail] Bags must be left at the front desk.","h":"عند مكتب الاستقبال."},{"n":24,"s":"What should visitors do with the ticket?","o":["keep it until they leave","give it to a guard","throw it away at the door","use it again tomorrow"],"k":0,"e":"[detail] Keep this ticket until you leave.","h":"الاحتفاظ بالتذكرة."},{"n":25,"s":"The rules on the ticket are mainly to …","o":["sell more tickets","help visitors find the café","protect the museum objects","teach history"],"k":2,"e":"[purpose] No touching, no flash, no bags — to protect the objects.","h":"حماية المعروضات."}]},{"l":["Text 6 (Questions 26–30): A note from Mum about dinner time","(65 words)","Turki,","I am at Grandma's house. Dinner is in the fridge — chicken and rice. Please heat it for three minutes in the microwave. We will eat at 8 o'clock when your father comes home. Don't forget to feed the cat. Your homework is on your desk; please finish it before dinner. If you need anything, call me on my mobile. Grandma sends her love.","Mum"],"q":[{"n":26,"s":"Where is Mum?","o":["at the supermarket","at work","at Grandma's house","in the kitchen"],"k":2,"e":"[detail] I am at Grandma's house.","h":"عند الجدة."},{"n":27,"s":"How long should Turki heat the food?","o":["three minutes","eight minutes","thirty minutes","one minute"],"k":0,"e":"[detail] heat it for three minutes.","h":"ثلاث دقائق."},{"n":28,"s":"Why will they eat at 8 o'clock?","o":["The food needs time to cook.","Turki's father comes home then.","Grandma is coming.","Turki has homework."],"k":1,"e":"[cause–effect] when your father comes home.","h":"عند عودة الأب."},{"n":29,"s":"What should Turki do before dinner?","o":["visit Grandma","cook the rice","wash the car","finish his homework"],"k":3,"e":"[detail] please finish it before dinner.","h":"إنهاء الواجب."},{"n":30,"s":"What is the main purpose of the note?","o":["to invite Turki to Grandma's","to give Turki instructions for the evening","to say sorry","to describe a recipe"],"k":1,"e":"[purpose] Mum tells Turki what to do this evening.","h":"إعطاء تعليمات."}]}],"n":30}],"sc":{},"review":{"quiz":[{"l":["Unit Review — 50 questions on new texts. Read each text and choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","مراجعة الوحدة: خمسون سؤالًا على نصوص جديدة، اقرأ كل نص واختر الإجابة الصحيحة.","Text 1 (Questions 1–5): The school bus driver","(63 words)","Mr. Saeed drives the school bus. He starts work at 5:30 every morning. First, he checks the tyres and cleans the windows. Then he drives to twelve houses and picks up the students. He always says good morning and smiles. The students like him very much. On the last day of school, they gave him a card and a box of dates."],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"What is the text mainly about?","o":["a kind school bus driver","the school day","twelve houses","a box of dates"],"k":0,"e":"[main idea · 1.1] The text describes Mr. Saeed and his work.","h":"النص عن السائق."},{"n":2,"s":"What time does Mr. Saeed start work?","o":["5:30","5:00","6:30","12:00"],"k":0,"e":"[detail · 1.2] He starts work at 5:30.","h":"الساعة 5:30."},{"n":3,"s":"What does he do first?","o":["picks up students","checks the tyres and cleans the windows","says good morning","drives to school"],"k":1,"e":"[detail · 1.5] First, he checks the tyres and cleans the windows.","h":"أولًا يفحص الإطارات."},{"n":4,"s":"The word 'him' in sentence 6 refers to …","o":["a student","the school","Mr. Saeed","the card"],"k":2,"e":"[reference · 1.4] The students like him → the driver.","h":"him تعود على السائق."},{"n":5,"s":"What did the students give him?","o":["a card and a box of dates","a new bus","flowers","a watch"],"k":0,"e":"[detail · 1.5] they gave him a card and a box of dates.","h":"بطاقة وتمر."}]},{"l":["Text 2 (Questions 6–10): A visit to a strawberry farm","(62 words)","Last Saturday, our class visited a strawberry farm near Tabuk. The farmer showed us long rows of green plants with bright red fruit. He taught us how to pick the strawberries gently so they did not get damaged. Each student filled a small basket. Then we washed the strawberries and ate some. They were sweet and juicy. It was a wonderful trip."],"q":[{"n":6,"s":"Which is the best title?","o":["How to Wash Fruit","Green Plants","The Farmer's House","A Class Trip to a Strawberry Farm"],"k":3,"e":"[best title · 1.1] The text is about the class visit to the farm.","h":"رحلة إلى مزرعة الفراولة."},{"n":7,"s":"The word gently is closest in meaning to …","o":["quickly","carefully and softly","noisily","angrily"],"k":1,"e":"[vocabulary in context · 1.3] so they did not get damaged → carefully.","h":"برفق."},{"n":8,"s":"The word juicy is closest in meaning to …","o":["very dry","very small","very cold","full of juice"],"k":3,"e":"[vocabulary in context · 1.3] sweet and juicy → full of juice.","h":"مليء بالعصير."},{"n":9,"s":"Where is the farm?","o":["near Riyadh","in the school","near Tabuk","near Abha"],"k":2,"e":"[detail · 1.2] a strawberry farm near Tabuk.","h":"قرب تبوك."},{"n":10,"s":"What did each student fill?","o":["a big box","a bottle","a bag of dates","a small basket"],"k":3,"e":"[detail · 1.5] Each student filled a small basket.","h":"سلة صغيرة."}]},{"l":["Text 3 (Questions 11–15): A boy who learns to ride a horse","(63 words)","Omar is eleven, and he is learning to ride a horse. Every Friday, his uncle takes him to a riding club. The horse is called Barq, which means lightning in Arabic. At first, Omar was frightened because Barq was very big. Now he is not afraid. He can sit up straight and hold the reins. His teacher says he is making good progress."],"q":[{"n":11,"s":"What is the text mostly about?","o":["a boy learning to ride a horse","the meaning of lightning","a riding club's prices","Omar's uncle's job"],"k":0,"e":"[main idea · 1.1] The text is about Omar's riding lessons.","h":"تعلّم ركوب الخيل."},{"n":12,"s":"Who takes Omar to the riding club?","o":["his father","his teacher","his uncle","his brother"],"k":2,"e":"[detail · 1.5] his uncle takes him to a riding club.","h":"عمه."},{"n":13,"s":"The word frightened is closest in meaning to …","o":["happy","tired","angry","afraid"],"k":3,"e":"[vocabulary in context · 1.3] The next sentence says Now he is not afraid.","h":"خائف."},{"n":14,"s":"The word 'he' in the last sentence refers to …","o":["the teacher","Barq","the uncle","Omar"],"k":3,"e":"[reference · 1.4] His teacher says he is making progress → Omar.","h":"he تعود على عمر."},{"n":15,"s":"Why was Omar frightened at first?","o":["Barq was very big.","Barq ran too fast.","The club was far away.","His teacher was angry."],"k":0,"e":"[cause–effect · 1.5] because Barq was very big.","h":"لأن الحصان كبير."}]},{"l":["Text 4 (Questions 16–20): Morning exercise in the park","(66 words)","Morning Walking Group — King Abdullah Park","Every day: 6:00 a.m. – 7:00 a.m.","Meeting point: the main gate","Free for everyone over 12 years old","Bring water and wear comfortable shoes.","Leader: Mr. Khaled (050 765 4321)","On the last Thursday of every month, we walk around the big lake.","No pets, please.","Join us and start your day in a healthy way!"],"q":[{"n":16,"s":"What is the purpose of this notice?","o":["to sell sports shoes","to close the park","to invite people to join a walking group","to find a new leader"],"k":2,"e":"[purpose · 1.6] Join us and start your day in a healthy way!","h":"دعوة للانضمام."},{"n":17,"s":"Where do the walkers meet?","o":["at the main gate","at the car park","at Mr. Khaled's house","at the lake"],"k":0,"e":"[detail · 1.2] Meeting point: the main gate.","h":"البوابة الرئيسة."},{"n":18,"s":"How much does it cost?","o":["12 riyals","7 riyals","50 riyals","nothing"],"k":3,"e":"[detail · 1.2] Free for everyone over 12.","h":"مجاني."},{"n":19,"s":"What should people bring?","o":["water","food","a ball","a bicycle"],"k":0,"e":"[detail · 1.6] Bring water and wear comfortable shoes.","h":"الماء."},{"n":20,"s":"Who can join the group?","o":["only children","anyone older than 12","only park workers","anyone under 12"],"k":1,"e":"[detail · 1.6] Free for everyone over 12 years old.","h":"من تجاوز 12 سنة."}]},{"l":["Text 5 (Questions 21–25): A lost house key","(71 words)","Yesterday, I lost my house key. I looked in my bag, my pockets and under my bed, but I could not find it. I was worried because my parents were at work. I called my best friend, but he did not know what to do. Then my little sister laughed and said, \"Look at the door!\" The key was still in the lock. I felt silly, but I was also relieved."],"q":[{"n":21,"s":"What is the text mainly about?","o":["a girl's bag","a lost key that was in the door","parents at work","a funny sister's game"],"k":1,"e":"[main idea · 1.1] The text tells the story of looking for the key.","h":"قصة المفتاح."},{"n":22,"s":"Where was the key?","o":["under the bed","in the bag","in the door lock","in a pocket"],"k":2,"e":"[detail · 1.5] The key was still in the lock.","h":"في القفل."},{"n":23,"s":"The word 'it' in sentence 2 refers to …","o":["the key","the bag","the bed","the house"],"k":0,"e":"[reference · 1.4] I could not find it → the key.","h":"it تعود على المفتاح."},{"n":24,"s":"The word worried is closest in meaning to …","o":["anxious","bored","proud","sleepy"],"k":0,"e":"[vocabulary in context · 1.3] Parents were at work and the key was lost → anxious.","h":"قلق."},{"n":25,"s":"The word relieved means the writer felt …","o":["angry with her sister","happy because the problem was over","afraid of the door","tired after work"],"k":1,"e":"[vocabulary in context · 1.3] Finding the key ended the problem.","h":"ارتاح."}]},{"l":["Text 6 (Questions 26–30): A new bakery on our street","(61 words)","A new bakery opened on our street last week. It is called Golden Bread. It opens at 5:00 a.m., so people can buy fresh bread for breakfast. The bakery sells Arabic bread, croissants and date cakes. The owner, Mr. Ibrahim, is from Jordan. Every morning there is a long queue outside, because the bread is hot and very cheap."],"q":[{"n":26,"s":"What is the name of the bakery?","o":["Fresh Bread","Mr. Ibrahim's","Date Cakes","Golden Bread"],"k":3,"e":"[detail · 1.2] It is called Golden Bread.","h":"الخبز الذهبي."},{"n":27,"s":"When does the bakery open?","o":["at 7:00 a.m.","at noon","at 5:00 a.m.","at 5:00 p.m."],"k":2,"e":"[detail · 1.2] It opens at 5:00 a.m.","h":"الخامسة صباحًا."},{"n":28,"s":"The word queue is closest in meaning to …","o":["a big oven","a bag of bread","a line of people waiting","a small table"],"k":2,"e":"[vocabulary in context · 1.3] a long queue outside … people wait.","h":"طابور."},{"n":29,"s":"Why is there a long queue every morning?","o":["The bread is hot and cheap.","The bakery is very small.","The owner is from Jordan.","It is near a school."],"k":0,"e":"[cause–effect · 1.5] because the bread is hot and very cheap.","h":"السبب."},{"n":30,"s":"The word 'It' in sentence 2 refers to …","o":["the street","the bread","the week","the bakery"],"k":3,"e":"[reference · 1.4] It is called Golden Bread → the bakery.","h":"It تعود على المخبز."}]},{"l":["Text 7 (Questions 31–35): Brushing teeth before bed","(67 words)","Dear Students,","Please brush your teeth for two minutes every night before bed. Use a soft toothbrush and a little toothpaste. Do not eat or drink anything after brushing, only water. Change your toothbrush every three months. Eat fruit and vegetables instead of sweets. Drink plenty of water every day. Visit the dentist twice a year. Healthy teeth help you eat, speak and smile!","— The School Nurse"],"q":[{"n":31,"s":"Who wrote this text?","o":["the school nurse","a student","a dentist from a shop","the head teacher"],"k":0,"e":"[detail · 1.6] — The School Nurse.","h":"ممرضة المدرسة."},{"n":32,"s":"What is the purpose of the text?","o":["to sell toothbrushes","to invite students to a party","to give advice about healthy teeth","to explain a new school rule about food"],"k":2,"e":"[purpose · 1.6] The text gives tips for healthy teeth.","h":"نصائح لصحة الأسنان."},{"n":33,"s":"How long should students brush their teeth?","o":["three minutes","ten minutes","one minute","two minutes"],"k":3,"e":"[detail · 1.2] brush your teeth for two minutes.","h":"دقيقتان."},{"n":34,"s":"What can students drink after brushing?","o":["milk","juice","only water","nothing at all"],"k":2,"e":"[detail · 1.5] Do not eat or drink anything after brushing, only water.","h":"الماء فقط."},{"n":35,"s":"How often should you change your toothbrush?","o":["every week","every three months","every year","every night"],"k":1,"e":"[detail · 1.2] Change your toothbrush every three months.","h":"كل ثلاثة أشهر."}]},{"l":["Text 8 (Questions 36–40): A football match on Friday","(61 words)","Our school football team played a big match on Friday. The other team was very strong, and at half-time the score was 0–1. In the second half, our captain, Bandar, scored two goals. The fans in the stadium cheered loudly. We won 2–1! After the match, the coach thanked every player. It was the happiest day of the season."],"q":[{"n":36,"s":"What is the text mainly about?","o":["a strong team from another city","a football match that our team won","the coach's job","a big stadium"],"k":1,"e":"[main idea · 1.1] The text describes the match and the win.","h":"عن المباراة والفوز."},{"n":37,"s":"What was the score at half-time?","o":["2–1","1–1","0–1","0–0"],"k":2,"e":"[detail · 1.5] at half-time the score was 0–1.","h":"0–1."},{"n":38,"s":"Who scored two goals?","o":["the coach","a fan","the other team","Bandar"],"k":3,"e":"[detail · 1.5] our captain, Bandar, scored two goals.","h":"بندر."},{"n":39,"s":"The word cheered is closest in meaning to …","o":["sat quietly","shouted happily","left early","cried"],"k":1,"e":"[vocabulary in context · 1.3] The fans cheered loudly → shouted happily.","h":"هتف."},{"n":40,"s":"The word 'It' in the last sentence refers to …","o":["the day of the match","the stadium","the coach","the score"],"k":0,"e":"[reference · 1.4] It was the happiest day → that Friday.","h":"It تعود على اليوم."}]},{"l":["Text 9 (Questions 41–45): A letter from a pen pal in Malaysia","(65 words)","Dear Sara,","Thank you for your letter. I live in Kuala Lumpur, the capital of Malaysia. It is hot and rainy here all year. My favourite food is nasi lemak — rice with coconut milk. I have two brothers. At school, I study Malay, English and Arabic. Please send me a photo of your school. I hope we can meet one day.","Your pen pal, Aisha"],"q":[{"n":41,"s":"Why did Aisha write this letter?","o":["to invite Sara to Malaysia next week","to reply to her pen pal and tell her about herself","to ask for food","to complain about the rain"],"k":1,"e":"[purpose · 1.6] She thanks Sara and describes her life.","h":"رد وتعريف بنفسها."},{"n":42,"s":"Where does Aisha live?","o":["in Riyadh","in Kuala Lumpur","in Jeddah","in Cairo"],"k":1,"e":"[detail · 1.2] I live in Kuala Lumpur.","h":"كوالالمبور."},{"n":43,"s":"What is nasi lemak?","o":["a kind of fish","a Malaysian school","rice with coconut milk","a sweet drink"],"k":2,"e":"[detail · 1.5] nasi lemak — rice with coconut milk.","h":"أرز بحليب جوز الهند."},{"n":44,"s":"What does Aisha ask Sara to send?","o":["a photo of her school","a letter in Arabic","a book","some dates"],"k":0,"e":"[detail · 1.6] Please send me a photo of your school.","h":"صورة المدرسة."},{"n":45,"s":"In 'It is hot and rainy here', the word 'It' refers to …","o":["the letter","the school","the food","the weather in Kuala Lumpur"],"k":3,"e":"[reference · 1.4] It is hot and rainy here → the weather there.","h":"It تعود على الطقس."}]},{"l":["Text 10 (Questions 46–50): Washing the family car","(68 words)","Every Saturday morning, my brothers and I wash the family car. First, we take everything out of it. Then we wash the outside with soap and water. My little brother cleans the wheels because he likes the bubbles. Finally, we dry the car with soft towels. Our father gives each of us ten riyals. My mother brings us cold juice when we finish. The car looks like new!"],"q":[{"n":46,"s":"Which is the best title?","o":["Soap and Bubbles","Washing the Family Car Together","Ten Riyals","A New Car"],"k":1,"e":"[best title · 1.1] The text describes the brothers washing the car.","h":"غسل السيارة معًا."},{"n":47,"s":"What do they do first?","o":["wash the wheels","dry the car","take everything out of the car","get ten riyals"],"k":2,"e":"[sequence · 1.5] First, we take everything out of it.","h":"الخطوة الأولى."},{"n":48,"s":"Why does the little brother clean the wheels?","o":["He is the tallest.","He likes the bubbles.","His father asks him.","The wheels are easy."],"k":1,"e":"[cause–effect · 1.5] because he likes the bubbles.","h":"يحب الفقاعات."},{"n":49,"s":"The word 'it' in sentence 2 refers to …","o":["the morning","the car","the soap","the water"],"k":1,"e":"[reference · 1.4] take everything out of it → the car.","h":"it تعود على السيارة."},{"n":50,"s":"The phrase looks like new means the car …","o":["is very old","is a new model","needs more washing","looks very clean"],"k":3,"e":"[vocabulary in context · 1.3] After washing, it looks clean, like a new car.","h":"يبدو نظيفًا جدًا."}]}],"n":50}};
